# Used only by the *blocking* CRITICAL-severity trivy step in
# .github/workflows/ci-security.yml -- the informational CRITICAL+HIGH
# report earlier in that job does NOT use this file, so everything below
# still shows up there for visibility. Every entry here is something we
# cannot fix ourselves; each has a plan for re-checking it, not a
# permanent blanket exemption.

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh auth bypass (unenforced source-address
# restrictions) -- a transitive dependency baked into pre-built upstream
# Go binaries this Dockerfile downloads as release artifacts (nuclei,
# httpx, subfinder), not something we build or vendor ourselves. Fixing
# it requires each upstream project (projectdiscovery/nuclei, /httpx,
# /subfinder) to cut a new release against golang.org/x/crypto >= 0.55.0.
# Re-check and remove this line once they have.
CVE-2026-56854

# crypto/tls: incorrect certificate validation during TLS session
# resumption -- same situation: baked into subfinder's own upstream Go
# toolchain build, not ours to patch directly. Re-check once
# projectdiscovery/subfinder ships a build against a patched Go stdlib.
CVE-2025-68121
